# Who has to review what.
#
# `docs/lifecycle.md` says only the user approves a spec, and `docs/constitution.md`
# says amending a principle needs explicit human approval. These lines are those two
# rules, expressed where GitHub can act on them: a pull request touching any of these
# paths requests a review from the owner automatically.
#
# Enabling "Require review from Code Owners" in the rulesets turns the request into a
# requirement. Do that once a second person has write access — GitHub does not let an
# author approve their own pull request, so a sole maintainer would block their own
# merges. Until then this file documents the authority and assigns the reviewer.

